derstands complicated tech (from earlier). D solves problems extremely well, concentration. B good at weather assessment, computer skills.\n\nCalmness under pressure: B handles stress well. C keeps calm in crisis (from earlier). D responds adequately. A not mentioned.\n\nDecision-making: A anticipates dangerous situations, sees connections. C makes correct decisions quickly. D solves problems extremely well.\n\nTeamwork/communication: A leadership but unfriendly. B pretentious, wrong tone. C puts concern for others above everything, creates positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. D moody, loner.\n\nProfessional development: C not willing to further education (negative). A eats unhealthily (maybe health). B conscientious (maybe good). D no info.\n\nThus overall, C seems best due to reliability, calmness, positive crew atmosphere, concern for others, but communication difficulty and lack of further education are concerns. A has strong technical but poor teamwork. D strong problem solving but poor teamwork. B good stress handling but poor teamwork.\n\nThus provisional preference: Candidate C.\n\nWe should also ask other agents for missing info: maybe ask about Candidate A's teamwork strengths beyond leadership? Or D's leadership strengths? But we have to produce a public message now. We can also ask a targeted question using tool to get more info from other agents. The instruction says we can ask other agents using tools. We could ask Agent 1 or Agent 2 for any positive teamwork/communication strengths for A or D. But we already have some info: A leadership qualities (positive). D takes responsibility seriously (positive). But maybe we want more details. However we need to produce a public message now. We could also include a question to other agents.\n\nThe format: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: ... METADATA_JSON: {\"agent\":\"agent_3\",\"vote\":\"Candidate C\"}.\n\nWe should summarize key evidence, alternatives, tradeoffs, uncertainties, what would chan